course: dictionary
lesson: 3926
title: Frothy: two meanings
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning, and frothy has two. The first is literal: covered in froth, which is a mass of tiny bubbles. «The Maya and Aztecs made a bitter, frothy chocolate drink» means the drink was full of bubbles.
explain: The second meaning is about a feeling or a kind of story. A frothy film or story is light and fun, and not serious. To check which meaning fits, swap your idea into the sentence and see if it still makes sense.
explain: Look at the words around frothy for clues. «In Mexico and Central America cocoa was drunk bitter, frothy and sometimes spicy.» Bitter and spicy tell you about taste, so frothy is describing how the drink looked and felt, with its bubbles.
fact: Frothy means covered in or full of froth, a mass of tiny bubbles.
fact: Frothy can also mean light and fun but not serious, like a frothy film or story.
fact: «Frothy milk» and «frothy waves» use the bubbly meaning.
fact: In science, froth forms when gas bubbles are trapped in a liquid, such as when bicarbonate of soda and vinegar are mixed.
fact: In stories, a frothy mouth on an animal can be a sign of illness, so do not touch.
exercise: «The Maya and Aztecs made a bitter, frothy chocolate drink.» What does frothy mean here? | Cold as ice | *Full of tiny bubbles | Very serious | Made from old beans
exercise: Mia says the new film is frothy. What might she mean? | It is very old | It is made of soap | *It is light and fun, not serious | It is covered in tiny bubbles
exercise: In science class, the mixture gave off gas and went frothy. Why? | *Gas bubbles were trapped in the liquid | The liquid turned into ice | The mixture was very old | Someone added sugar only
test: Which meaning of frothy fits «frothy coffee»? | *Covered in tiny bubbles | Bitter and spicy | Light and fun, not serious | Very old
test: Which sentence uses frothy to mean light and fun? | *«The movie was a frothy comedy with silly jokes.» | «The frothy bubble bath was warm.» | «The frothy milk sat on top.» | «Frothy waves hit the sand.»
exam: In «frothy coffee», what does frothy describe? | The time it was made | *The bubbles on top of the drink | The colour of the cup | The taste of the coffee
